cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Lattice Theta Functions with Half-Integral Characteristics"
abstract: >-
  Exact proofs, certificates, and reproducible computations for identical
  vanishing of lattice theta functions with half-integral characteristics.
  The symmetry converse holds in ranks one through three and fails in rank
  four. Rank-four results: an identically vanishing even characteristic of a
  lattice of determinant 1729 whose two coset lattices are the Conway-Sloane
  isospectral pair, which are not isometric; a counterexample to the symmetry
  converse of determinant 1156 with automorphism group {I, -I}, improving the
  original determinant-23716 example (bracket 24 < det <= 1156, no minimality
  claim); and the rank-four parity property, which fails for indecomposable
  odd lattices of determinant 49 not divisible by four and for even
  indecomposable lattices of odd determinant at determinant 121, with
  complete class lists and structural theorems. The release also includes
  the low-rank parity classification, the irreducible crystallographic root
  lattices in the stated normalization, exact determinant-at-most-24 censuses
  through rank four, and a checked literature note on isospectral lattices.
  No literature-priority claim is made.
